# Environment and dependency folders
# Convention (CL-03): `.env.example` (root) is the single TRACKED template; per-host
# secrets live in `env.local` / `.env.local` (never committed). Do not re-add the old
# per-area templates (env.grm.example; channels/ticketing-ui/.env.local is covered by
# that package's own .gitignore).
# ⚠ Two deliberate additions, DPG-16 (2026-08-18): `.env.open` and `.env.openai` are tracked,
# secret-free templates showing the SAME system pointed at two providers. They are not per-area
# templates — they are the artefact a DPG reviewer diffs to see that switching provider is an
# environment change (indicator 4). A test asserts both carry no key and declare identical
# variables. `.env` (exact match, above) does not cover them; that was checked, not assumed.
create_env.sh
env.local
env.local.example
.env.local
aws_local.local
*.aws.local
.env
